	"ResourceName": "okta_user_allowlist",
	"Description": "Suppress Okta alerts for an account, as actor or as the person acted on.\n\nColumns: key,enabled,until_ymd,reason\nKey: \u003clogin\u003e|\u003cdetection name\u003e for one detection, or \u003clogin\u003e|* for all. until_ymd (YYYYMMDD, optional): stop suppressing after this date.\n\nThe detection name is the scheduled search name after the group, e.g. \"Okta Admin Console Access from a New IP\". Logins are lowercase and without @domain. Rows with enabled = 0 are ignored; the shipped rows are disabled examples. Used by every Okta detection and the modification feed through $OKTA_USER_TUNING / $OKTA_IP_TUNING.",
